## Design: Sender-Allow Scoping for OTLP Ingress (4317/4318)

**Summary:** The Phase 0 harvest shows a brownfield baseline of `allow all;` on both OTLP server blocks in `otlp-ingress.conf`, with no other sender restriction on those ports. The crossing value `exporterCidrBlock = 10.99.0.0/27` (published by FABRIC, chained via DAG edge) becomes the sole permitted sender on 4317 and 4318, replacing `allow all` in both blocks. `operator-access.conf` (port 14318) and the collector's own config are out of scope and untouched, per the harvest's own scoping annotation and the Program Interface Contract's `ingressScope`.

---

### Baseline facts carried forward verbatim (source: Phase 0 Harvester, `get_ingress_config`, "as-deployed files (ro mount)")

**File 1 — `otlp-ingress.conf` (the ONLY file this change touches):**
```nginx
# OTLP ingress allowlist — the lab's enforcement point for "which senders may export telemetry".
# Fronts BOTH OTLP receivers: gRPC (4317) and HTTP (4318). The collector accepts OTLP only on a
# private network shared with this proxy, so these two server blocks are the only way in.
# nginx evaluates allow/deny IN ORDER, first match wins.

# OTLP/gRPC
server {
    listen 4317;
    http2 on;

    location / {
        allow all;

        grpc_pass grpc://172.31.114.10:4317;
    }
}

# OTLP/http
server {
    listen 4318;
    client_max_body_size 16m;

    location / {
        allow all;

        proxy_pass http://172.31.114.10:4318;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $remote_addr;
    }
}
```
Current sender-allow: **NONE** — `allow all;`, no `deny`, on both blocks.

**File 2 — `operator-access.conf` (OUT OF SCOPE — must not be modified):**
```nginx
server {
    listen 14318;
    client_max_body_size 16m;

    location / {
        allow 172.20.0.1;
        deny all;

        proxy_pass http://172.31.114.10:4318;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
    }
}
```
Already restricted to `172.20.0.1`; explicitly annotated by the harvest as rig plumbing, not the sender allowlist. Left untouched.

**Collector config (`get_otel_config`, as-deployed file mount)** — OTLP receiver bound to `172.31.114.10:4317`/`:4318` on the private network reachable only via `obs-ingress`; **no design change required** here — the collector has no source-IP enforcement capability, and `otlp-ingress.conf` is confirmed as the sole enforcement point.

