| Leaving `allow all;` and adding per-source `deny` entries for everything else | Infeasible against an unbounded, unenumerable "everything else" sender universe; also does not satisfy contract wording ("becomes the sole permitted sender") which requires an allow-list model, not a deny-list model | No — does not meet the contract |

If the exporter range published by FABRIC changes in a later run (device re-harvest, interface added/removed), the operator must re-derive via the FABRIC leg and re-author this file — the ordering pattern itself does not need to change, only the CIDR literal.

